 "result_text": "`DefFrame` now supports `CHANNEL-DELAY`.\n\nI ran one check: parsing `DEFFRAME 0 \"rf\":` with `CHANNEL-DELAY: 1e-7` gives a `DefFrame` with `channel_delay=1e-07`, and printing the program writes the attribute back out. I didn't run the test suite.\n\n- **Construction:** `DefFrame` has a new optional `channel_delay` field, which `out()` writes as `CHANNEL-DELAY`. The change is in `pyquil/quilbase.py`.\n- **Parsing:** the grammar accepts `CHANNEL-DELAY` as a frame attribute, and the parser maps it to `channel_delay`. These changes are in `pyquil/_parser/grammar.lark` and `pyquil/_parser/parser.py`.\n- **Reserved word:** I also added `\"CHANNEL-DELAY\"` to the reserved-words list in `quilbase.py`, next to `\"INITIAL-FREQUENCY\"`. I didn't check whether anything else relies on that list.\n\nI didn't commit anything or touch any tests.",
